.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Beyond nearest-neighbor spacing, the number variance \Sigma^2(L) -- the variance of the eigenvalue count in a randomly placed window of (unfolded) length L -- probes longer-range spectral correlations. An uncorrelated (Poisson) sequence has \Sigma^2(L) = L; level repulsion makes the Gaussian ensembles&#x27; spectra far more rigid, with only logarithmic growth (Dyson-Mehta 1963):">

